  {
   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Packaging of DNA"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "In prokaryotes the negatively charged DNA is held with positively charged proteins in the nucleoid. In eukaryotes, DNA wraps around a histone octamer, rich in the basic amino acids lysine and arginine, to form a nucleosome of about 200 bp. Repeating nucleosomes form a 'beads-on-string' chromatin fibre, which coils further into chromosomes with the help of non-histone chromosomal (NHC) proteins. Loosely packed, lightly staining euchromatin is transcriptionally active; densely packed, darkly staining heterochromatin is inactive.",
    "kn": "ಯೂಕ್ಯಾರಿಯೋಟ್‌ಗಳಲ್ಲಿ DNA ಹಿಸ್ಟೋನ್ ಅಷ್ಟಕದ ಸುತ್ತ ಸುತ್ತಿ ಸುಮಾರು 200 ಕ್ಷಾರ ಜೊತೆಗಳ ನ್ಯೂಕ್ಲಿಯೋಸೋಮ್ ಆಗುತ್ತದೆ. ಯೂಕ್ರೊಮ್ಯಾಟಿನ್ ಸಕ್ರಿಯ, ಹೆಟೆರೊಕ್ರೊಮ್ಯಾಟಿನ್ ನಿಷ್ಕ್ರಿಯ."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "Histone octamer: lysine and arginine (+ve)"
    },
    {
     "en": "Nucleosome ≈ 200 bp"
    },
    {
     "en": "Euchromatin active; heterochromatin inactive"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "In prokaryotes the negatively charged DNA is held with positively charged proteins in the nucleoid. In eukaryotes, DNA wraps around a histone octamer, rich in the basic amino acids lysine and arginine, to form a nucleosome of about 200 bp. Repeating nucleosomes form a 'beads-on-string' chromatin fibre, which coils further into chromosomes with the help of non-histone chromosomal (NHC) proteins. Loosely packed, lightly staining euchromatin is transcriptionally active; densely packed, darkly staining heterochromatin is inactive.",
    "kn": "ಯೂಕ್ಯಾರಿಯೋಟ್‌ಗಳಲ್ಲಿ DNA ಹಿಸ್ಟೋನ್ ಅಷ್ಟಕದ ಸುತ್ತ ಸುತ್ತಿ ಸುಮಾರು 200 ಕ್ಷಾರ ಜೊತೆಗಳ ನ್ಯೂಕ್ಲಿಯೋಸೋಮ್ ಆಗುತ್ತದೆ. ಯೂಕ್ರೊಮ್ಯಾಟಿನ್ ಸಕ್ರಿಯ, ಹೆಟೆರೊಕ್ರೊಮ್ಯಾಟಿನ್ ನಿಷ್ಕ್ರಿಯ."
